{"id": "EUVD-2026-108633", "enisaUuid": "bc440396-78f2-3337-b42e-48fb2ab37ab2", "description": "`JwksTrustStore.Get` assigned each parsed key to the function's **named return value** while refreshing the JWKS cache. When the requested `kid` was not present, the trailing naked `return` handed the caller the last key in the JWKS document together with a `nil` error \u2014 a confidently wrong answer instead of \"not found\".", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T08:40:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T08:40:55", "baseScore": 6.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/eclipse-keypont/gose/security/advisories/GHSA-v7r8-g6h9-99vv"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89313"], "assigner": "eclipse", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "80af4bd0-6b8c-3c68-94c7-2585a6286906", "product": {"name": "Eclipse KeyPont - GOSE", "vendor": {"name": "Eclipse Foundation"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.0.0-rc4"}, {"id": "dbb73aae-d668-3bb6-83cd-82d91b5cd120", "product": {"name": "Eclipse KeyPont - GOSE", "vendor": {"name": "Eclipse Foundation"}}, "product_version": "0.7.5 \u22640.13.0-rc1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "59e9d354-8aef-3e60-a226-2b649ffd608a", "vendor": {"name": "Eclipse Foundation"}}], "isExploited": false}